# Workspace grouping-directory .envrc
#
# Every directory in the git workspace that groups repositories (the root and
# each visibility, owner and family directory) has an .envrc that is a symlink
# to this file. home-manager installs it from nix-home
# (modules/home-manager/direnv/workspace.envrc) and creates the symlinks on
# every switch. Change it there, never through a symlink.
#
# Why: repositories sit several levels below the workspace root, and each one's
# own .envrc sets up its dev shell (nix flake, tools, exported variables). A
# shell or AI agent session started in a directory above them used to get none
# of that, so a session in a family directory could not run the tools its
# repositories need.
#
# What: `use children` sources every child directory's .envrc. Grouping
# directories below this one run this same file, so starting at any level
# loads every repository beneath it, plus their MCP servers and Claude Code
# plugins. How it does that: modules/home-manager/direnv/use-children.sh.

# Additions for this directory only (for example a dev shell all its children
# share). Not version controlled; keep it next to the symlink. Loaded before
# the children, which see it without calling source_up.
source_env_if_exists .envrc.local

use children
